### 1. Task outcome (short version):
I extracted all occurrences of "Adjusted EBITDA" and their reconciliations from the provided Prospectus and Annual Report excerpts for Link Mobility Group Holding ASA. Key findings:
- Prospectus (LINK_prospectus_main): Reporting currency NOK; units generally in NOK (thousands) or NOK million depending on table. Adjusted EBITDA definitions and adjustments: "EBITDA adjusted for mergers and acquisitions costs, restructuring costs and costs related to share option program." Numerical Adjusted EBITDA (group-level) disclosed for: Six months ended 30 June 2020 (182.6 / 182,645 / 182,692 depending on table/units), Six months 2019 (134.2 / 134,183 / 134,306), Year ended 2019 (307.5 / 307,548 / 307,941), Year 2018 (212.0 / 212,370 / 212,424), Year 2017 (140.0 / 139,988 / 139,??). LTM Adjusted EBITDA (30 June 2020) = 356.1 (NOK million). Segment-level Adjusted EBITDA (NOK 1,000) in prospectus table.
- Annual Report 2020 (LINK Annual Report 2020): Reporting currency NOK; amounts presented in NOK (thousand or million in headings). Adjusted EBITDA definition: "EBITDA adjusted by expenses related to significant one-time, non-recurring events such as acquisitions and restructuring activities, legal advisors, and share-based compensation." Group-level Adjusted EBITDA: 2020 = 390,841 (or 390,842 in some tables) (NOK thousand or NOK in notes), 2019 = 307,549 / 307,941 / 307,549; Adjusted EBITDA margin 2020 = 11.0%, 2019 = 10.6% (also 10.5%/10.1% in prospectus). Segment-level Adjusted EBITDA per segment for 2020 and 2019 also provided (e.g., Northern/Nordics 240,485 vs 194,266 etc.). Reconciliations provided: Adjusted EBITDA less Non-recurring items and depreciation to arrive at Operating profit (EBIT). Non-recurring items explained and examples given; share-based compensation appears as an adjustment in 2020 in Annual Report (34,711) but not in Prospectus where share option cost sometimes shown as "-" for certain tables. LTM, pro forma references: Prospectus includes LTM Adjusted EBITDA (356.1), Annual Report includes a forward-looking pro forma adjusted EBITDA margin guidance (13-15% for 2024). 
- Restatements/notes: Prospectus/Annual Report note that amounts are presented in NOK and in thousands unless stated; tables show slight numeric differences likely due to rounding or different unit headings (NOK million vs NOK 1,000). Certain tables indicate adjustments extracted from payroll and other operating expense line items and note amounts by period (NOK thousands listed). Prior period comparatives noted adjustments due to adoption of IAS33/IFRS8 and segment presentation; no explicit restatement of historical adjusted EBITDA totals other than reconciliations and rounding differences. Page/table references: I captured table headings and surrounding text from the provided excerpts; specific page numbers in excerpts include Prospectus pages ~18, 55, 78, 82 and Annual Report pages ~22, 23, 53, 54, 81, 82.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
